# Suki, Kyoshi Warrior ({2}{G/W}{G/W}, */4): "Suki's power is equal to the number of creatures you control" counts only Bot1's creatures
# (Bot2's Ornithopter adds nothing: Suki is a 1/4 on turn 3 before attacking). "Whenever Suki attacks, create a 1/1 white Ally
# creature token that's tapped and attacking" (CR 508.4): the Ally arrives tapped and attacking Bot2, raising Suki to 2/4, so Bot2 takes
# 2 + 1. The Ally was never declared as an attacker, so Suki does not trigger a second time (only one Ally is made).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Suki, Kyoshi Warrior
Plains x4
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Suki, Kyoshi Warrior.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Suki, Kyoshi Warrior.Power = 1
Bot1.Attack(Suki, Kyoshi Warrior > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Combat.Attackers = Suki, Kyoshi Warrior > Bot2; Ally Token > Bot2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Suki, Kyoshi Warrior.Power = 2
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Battlefield.Ally Token.Tapped = True
Bot1.Battlefield = Ally Token; Mox Pearl; Suki, Kyoshi Warrior
